   $q$Diego is writing a letter to the city council asking for a crosswalk on Pine Avenue near Diego's school. Which sentence best keeps a formal, respectful tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"You guys seriously need to put a crosswalk on Pine Avenue.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"Please, please, please put a crosswalk on Pine Avenue!!!","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-punctuation"},{"text":"Anyone who thinks about it for one second knows Pine Avenue needs a crosswalk.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"insulting-tone"},{"text":"A crosswalk on Pine Avenue would allow students to cross safely on their way to school.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A crosswalk on Pine Avenue would allow students to cross safely on their way to school.$q$, $q$The correct sentence gives a clear reason in calm, formal language. The "one second" sentence avoids slang, but it talks down to the council members, which is not respectful.$q$, 'draft', null)
